4013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+4}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "35d7d67a711e6e9e7b1e89ca7462dd3581856b6a9b88b39695ec1230c1c93fbe" "basis" 1164 "verifi