nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba6835924838d81122aa90d9a5c26b5dec67f7b1a06cd80083dbfbf39543c9c6"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+4}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+16}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-16}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2}=0$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =2x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{2x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{1}{2x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2(0)+C} \\\\ C & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\frac{2}{4x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba6835924838d81122aa90d9a5c26b5dec67f7b1a06cd80083dbfbf39543c9c6"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-347853" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{4x+1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-355576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ given that  $\\,y(0)=2.$\n\n$y(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡($\n{{field-1}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-355576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{0}+C) & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ C-\\frac{1}{2} & ={e}^{2} \\\\ C & =\\frac{2{e}^{2}+1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-2x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=2$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{-{e}^{-2x}+2{e}^{2}+1}{2}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-355576" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ba6835924838d81122aa90d9a5c26b5dec67f7b1a06cd80083dbfbf39543c9c6"} {"question" "q-355576" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14050314/state.json" "file_sha256" "1b083dbb847d3dfedf79fae411e6ca44f425417ff0dc1da3948e334a7aa2398e"} {"question" "q-355576" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "e^2+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{e^{-2x}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/1